From 26990198521905b1b20c9d7cb3829ff50e4c657f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ziyuw-Plank <236070466+ziyuw-Plank@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 18:16:20 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(desktop): Linux API-key UX, /opt/deepseek-harness, match
 Win Platform i18n

- Treat enterWorkspace failure after a successful credential save as non-fatal
  so welcome no longer shows "could not save" when the key is already on disk.
- On Linux, prefer official addApiKey / welcomeApiKey CTAs (same i18n keys and
  zh/en strings Windows uses) for bottom-left menu and welcome entry.
- Map Linux desktopPlatform to win32 so Host Platform headers match Windows
  (schema has no linux value; null previously fell back to web).
- Set Linux productName to deepseek-harness so FpmTarget installs under
  /opt/deepseek-harness while desktop Name stays "DeepSeek Harness".
---
